<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sierra Leone Creole people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Krio people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creoles</a>, or Krio, are descendants of the freed slaves who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a> from 1787: Black Poor from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, black Nova Scotians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaican-maroons">Jamaican Maroons</a> and tens of thousands of Africans liberated from slave ships by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>. Protestant and English-educated, they dominated the colony's professions and trade, and their English-based Krio language is Sierra Leone's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingua-franca">lingua franca</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sierra-leone-creole-people.jpg" alt="Sierra Leone Creole people" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adam Cuerden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samuel_Coleridge-Taylor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
